{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Second-review disposition: fixed all four blocking findings. The runner now preserves every current MODE route, owns BRIDGE_PAUSED parsing plus strict ticket commit/push, canonicalizes legacy benign 3/4/75 only at its wrapper boundary, and leaves direct legacy outputs unchanged. GHA explicitly retains RECONCILE_CONTINUOUS re-dispatch and the 20-minute schedule; Jenkins/GitLab use native scheduling. Enumerated every additional reconcile-bridge.yml consumer with retarget/preserve-as-is disposition. Added and recorded _ref_lock.read_pause_with_oid plus backend tests so the reason check and CAS delete use one OID snapshot. Split the affected compound ACs into independently observable contracts. The GitLab provenance/checksum advisory remains accepted with fail-closed retrieval verification."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786299772502462001,"uuid":"915fa064-a904-4a50-8786-a5029c14be1c"}